of four informative newsletters in reducing anxiety. Of these, 41 women were randomly selected to receive the           
newsletter. A follow-up assessment performed 4 months after the initial visit showed a significant improvement in the   
accuracy of perception of risk and a reduction of cancer anxiety, but no significant change in performance of BSE. The  
newsletters produced no significant effect."},                                                                          
        {"study_index": 26, "title": "Improving risk communication", "abstract": "This paper explores reasons for       
